# {{project_name}}

<!-- stacks:fill One or two sentences: what the app does and who it's for. -->

A native iPhone app in Swift and SwiftUI. `project.yml` defines the Xcode project; XcodeGen generates it.

## Toolchain

<!-- stacks:fill The versions recorded at setup: Xcode, iOS SDK, Swift, iOS deployment target, XcodeGen, SwiftLint. -->

Install the tools with `brew install xcodegen swiftlint xcbeautify` (swift-format ships with Xcode), then run `make doctor`.

## Getting started

```sh
make project     # generate the Xcode project from project.yml
make test        # unit tests on a simulator
open *.xcodeproj # run and debug in Xcode
```

`make help` lists every target. `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` covers simulators, signing and the project file; `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` covers how the app is put together.
